ao3(a,b){return"\u26a0\ufe0f You selected **"+a+"** but haven't set up the API Key for "+b+' yet.\n\n\ud83d\udc49 Please tap the model switch icon at top right and press **"Set API Key"** to get started \u2728'},
gao4(){return"\u26a0\ufe0f Running On-Device LLM models is not supported on Web. Please use the Android app or switch to **Satang Fast Engine**."},
gbad(){return'Hello! I\'m **Satang AI Assistant**, your on-device personal finance assistant \u2728\nRuns 100% offline and private\u2014your data is never sent outside your device \ud83d\udd12\n\nYou can ask questions freely, for example:\n\u2022 \ud83d\udcca *"Summarize this month\'s income and expenses"*\n\u2022 \ud83d\udcb0 *"Show every account balance"*\n\u2022 \ud83d\udcc8 *"Which category has the highest spending?"*\n\u2022 \ud83c\udfaf *"To save 100,000 in 1 year, how much should I save monthly?"*\n\u2022 \ud83d\udca1 *"Recommend a 50/30/20 budget allocation"*\n\u2022 \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f *"How large should my emergency fund be?"*\n\u2022 \ud83d\udcc5 *"How much can I still spend today?"*\n\u2022 \ud83d\udccb *"How do I export Excel or back up my data?"*'},
gb8P(){return"\ud83c\udfe6 **Manage accounts (add/edit):**\n1. Open **Accounts** from the bottom menu or left drawer.\n2. Tap **\u201c+ Add account.\u201d**\n3. Choose the account type (cash, bank, credit card, investment).\n4. Enter a name, choose an emoji, set the opening balance, and save."},
gb8S(){return"\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f **Create and manage categories:**\n1. Open **Categories**.\n2. Tap **\u201c+ Add category.\u201d**\n3. Choose expense or income.\n4. Choose an emoji and color, set a monthly budget, and save."},
gb8T(){return"\ud83d\udcca **Export Excel (.xlsx):**\n1. Open Settings or a report screen.\n2. Choose **Export Excel**.\n3. Select the period or accounts to export.\n4. Save the file; Satang organizes sheets by account and category."},
gb8Q(){return"\ud83d\udcbe **Back up and restore data:**\n1. Open Settings and choose **Backup data**.\n2. Export a password-protected `.zip` or `.json` backup.\n3. Import the file to restore it, or enable automatic sync with your private GitHub repository."},
gb8V(){return"\ud83d\udc65 **Split Bill:**\n1. Open the tools menu and choose **Split Bill**.\n2. Enter the total or add individual items.\n3. Add people and assign each person's share.\n4. Satang calculates the net amount and shows a QR code for payment."},
gb8R(){return"\ud83d\udcc5 **Sync with Google Calendar:**\n1. Open Settings and choose **Google Calendar**.\n2. Connect your Google account.\n3. Enable event sync and automatic due-bill reminders."},
gb8U(){return"\ud83d\udd10 **Security and app lock:**\n1. Open Settings and choose **Security & screen lock**.\n2. Set a 4-6 digit PIN.\n3. Enable biometrics (fingerprint or Face ID) for quick, secure unlocking."},
gb8M(){return"\ud83d\udcc8 **What is inflation, and how can I prepare?**\n\u2022 Inflation is a sustained rise in prices, reducing the purchasing power of the same amount of money.\n\u2022 **Practical responses:**\n  1. Avoid holding excessive idle cash for long periods.\n  2. Invest excess savings in suitable inflation-resistant assets such as diversified funds, stocks, gold, or property.\n  3. Review optional expenses regularly in Satang."},
gb8L(){return"\ud83d\udcb3 **Manage debt and credit cards:**\n1. **Pay in full and on time:** avoid high credit-card interest.\n2. **Pay down debt:** use the snowball method for small balances or the avalanche method for the highest interest rate.\n3. Avoid credit-card cash advances because fees and daily interest can apply immediately."},
gb8O(){return"\ud83e\uddfe **Common personal income-tax deductions:**\n1. **Personal/family:** personal, spouse, child, and parent allowances.\n2. **Insurance/savings:** life insurance, health insurance, and social security.\n3. **Long-term investment:** SSF, RMF, and Thai ESG subject to current annual limits.\n4. **Property/donations:** mortgage interest and eligible general or educational donations. Verify limits for the applicable tax year."},
gb8N(){return"\ud83d\udcca **Beginner investing principles:**\n1. Build 3-6 months of emergency savings first.\n2. **DCA:** invest a fixed amount regularly to average costs and reduce emotional decisions.\n3. Diversify through broad index or balanced funds.\n4. Invest only after understanding the product and its risks."},
b8r(a,b,c,d,e,f){return"\ud83d\udca1 **50/30/20 budget allocation**\n\nThe 50/30/20 rule divides income into:\n1. \ud83c\udfe0 **50% Needs:** `"+b+"` \u2014 housing, utilities, food, transport, insurance.\n2. \ud83d\udecd\ufe0f **30% Wants:** `"+c+"` \u2014 shopping, travel, dining, entertainment.\n3. \ud83d\udcb0 **20% Savings:** `"+d+"` \u2014 emergency savings, funds, investments, or debt payoff.\n\n\ud83d\udcca Calculated from income: `"+a+"`\n\ud83d\udccc Current monthly spending: `"+e+"`\n"+f},
gb8s(){return"\ud83d\udca1 **50/30/20 budget allocation**\n\n1. \ud83c\udfe0 **50% Needs:** housing, utilities, food, and transport.\n2. \ud83d\udecd\ufe0f **30% Wants:** shopping, travel, dining, and entertainment.\n3. \ud83d\udcb0 **20% Savings:** emergency savings, funds, and long-term investment."},
gb8t(){return"\ud83d\udfe2 Spending remains within the 80% spending limit, leaving room for the 20% savings target."},
gb8u(){return"\ud83d\udd34 Spending exceeds the 80% Needs + Wants limit. Review discretionary categories to restore the 20% savings target."},
b8G(a,b,c,d,e){return"\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f **Emergency fund plan**\n\nAn emergency fund should usually cover **3-6 months of expenses** for illness, job loss, or urgent repairs.\n\n\ud83d\udcca Based on average monthly expenses of `"+a+"`:\n\u2022 \ud83d\udfe1 **Minimum (3 months):** `"+b+"`\n\u2022 \ud83d\udfe2 **Recommended (6 months):** `"+c+"`\n\n\ud83d\udcb0 **Current net worth:** `"+d+"`\n"+e},
gb8H(){return"\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f **Emergency fund plan**\n\nKeep the emergency fund in a liquid, accessible account such as a high-interest savings account or money-market fund."},
gb8I(){return"\ud83c\udf1f Excellent. Your assets cover six months of expenses; surplus funds can be considered for long-term investing."},
